  "decision_conditions": [
    "The applicant should be aware of the additional information required for any future application:\r\n\r\nInclude a 'Schedule of Windows & Works': this should identify and include high-quality, high-resolution images of each window proposed for replacement. It should label each window and match that to the annotated drawings for clarity. If wholesale replacement is justified, then the replacement windows should demonstrably meet the following criteria: \r\n\r\n- The new conservation-type slim line double glazed units should be no more than c.12-14mm and avoid a spacer bar, or if that is necessary, the spacer should ideally be white foam to match the external finish. \r\n- Should be of a hand-painted white finish to match. \r\n\r\nOtherwise, the profile, form and detailed dimensions of the replacement units should be made clear (labelled) and should match as far as possible that of the existing windows. This is particularly important in terms of external elevational dimensions, recognising that some additional depth will be required in the plan. This should be made clear through existing and proposed detailed drawings for that particular window type."
